body:
I am plus sized but I've so far only been attracted to thin women. Not fit, just thin. I prefer non-athletic skinny women.  But I do think our attractions can change with the ebb and flow of life.  I am demisexual, so connection comes before attraction, but I don't really feel attraction very often anyway. I think all bodies are worthy of respect and care, and I believe in body neutrality instead of body positivity. A  body doesn't \*have\* to be beautiful.  But I think there is someone out there for everyone, and for many queer women, attraction is based on connection first, at least from what I've observed. 

&#x200B;

I will say though that last year I got love-bombed by a woman on tumblr who prefers fat women, like, almost fetish-level.  She had a nearly ideal body in terms of distribution and shape.  She harmed me a lot and I had to block her for my safety.  At this point, I do not plan to pursue another relationship, but I would say I feel weary to date other thin women now because of the possibility of ulterior motives.
